[[:db/add "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b" :answer/id #uuid "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b"] [:db/add "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b" :answer/value "-1"] [:db/ensure "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b" :answer/validate] [:db/add "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80" :answer-field/id #uuid "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80"] [:db/add "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80" :answer-field/choices "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b"] [:db/add "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80" :answer-field/correct "b00d144d-f59a-5556-84b9-682e7177c01b"] [:db/ensure "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228" :question/id #uuid "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228"] [:db/add "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/83/8334b8375ab70375fb7da06cc1a3ada7fa22940d0bf374e768a49bcb8162f75c.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228" :question/worked-solution "First trace $4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/7f/7fed06f512c08a83bb6f4fd71042a498832a6258bc0230b905283041e0dc3518.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $4$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{4}{4}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=4\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228" :question/answer-fields "03f585de-1181-502f-900c-9758026b8c80"] [:db/ensure "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "829954bd-19ff-5443-a56e-785466d98228"] [:db/add "e4342487-1dc0-5bf5-9eab-efefdddb8ecf" :answer/id #uuid "e4342487-1dc0-5bf5-9eab-efefdddb8ecf"] [:db/add "e4342487-1dc0-5bf5-9eab-efefdddb8ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e4342487-1dc0-5bf5-9eab-efefdddb8ecf" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}"] [:db/ensure "e4342487-1dc0-5bf5-9eab-efefdddb8ecf" :answer/validate] [:db/add "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802" :answer/id #uuid "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802"] [:db/add "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802" :answer/value "-4"] [:db/ensure "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802" :answer/validate] [:db/add "b864c613-7e68-5fe8-b29e-02e7471e1250" :answer/id #uuid "b864c613-7e68-5fe8-b29e-02e7471e1250"] [:db/add "b864c613-7e68-5fe8-b29e-02e7471e1250" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "b864c613-7e68-5fe8-b29e-02e7471e1250" :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}"] [:db/ensure "b864c613-7e68-5fe8-b29e-02e7471e1250" :answer/validate] [:db/add "390b5cae-e9a1-5c61-9f84-fd6e5b197d55" :answer/id #uuid "390b5cae-e9a1-5c61-9f84-fd6e5b197d55"] [:db/add "390b5cae-e9a1-5c61-9f84-fd6e5b197d55" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "390b5cae-e9a1-5c61-9f84-fd6e5b197d55" :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4}"] [:db/ensure "390b5cae-e9a1-5c61-9f84-fd6e5b197d55" :answer/validate] [:db/add "947d41af-fe15-5186-ac1b-f5a746db2bf2" :answer/id #uuid "947d41af-fe15-5186-ac1b-f5a746db2bf2"] [:db/add "947d41af-fe15-5186-ac1b-f5a746db2bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "947d41af-fe15-5186-ac1b-f5a746db2bf2" :answer/value "-16"] [:db/ensure "947d41af-fe15-5186-ac1b-f5a746db2bf2" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/choices "e4342487-1dc0-5bf5-9eab-efefdddb8ecf"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/choices "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/choices "b864c613-7e68-5fe8-b29e-02e7471e1250"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/choices "390b5cae-e9a1-5c61-9f84-fd6e5b197d55"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/choices "947d41af-fe15-5186-ac1b-f5a746db2bf2"] [:db/add "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/correct "292eb640-5c6d-5b42-bfc2-d7e225ef4802"] [:db/ensure "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5" :question/id #uuid "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5"] [:db/add "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/3b/3b0538fea2d3d7d88ce59a269d4800a158aaa46853cad019c417623193c62c95.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5" :question/worked-solution "First trace $3\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/04/04888a884d92d8db0b6b75931a796df39e6bd128f98c3e87c2d7b825203b4cb9.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $16$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{16}{4}=4$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-4\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+(-4\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-4$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5" :question/answer-fields "a80d1f92-fba9-5775-8226-91aa992b50f1"] [:db/ensure "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "1150b14c-bf4e-546a-8778-0b826485cbd5"] [:db/add "cc9bd585-f432-5898-9416-b0a89ccf8171" :answer/id #uuid "cc9bd585-f432-5898-9416-b0a89ccf8171"] [:db/add "cc9bd585-f432-5898-9416-b0a89ccf8171" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "cc9bd585-f432-5898-9416-b0a89ccf8171" :answer/value "-3"] [:db/ensure "cc9bd585-f432-5898-9416-b0a89ccf8171" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e494b272-971a-5081-b2ed-2bace2a15a45" :answer/id #uuid "e494b272-971a-5081-b2ed-2bace2a15a45"] [:db/add "e494b272-971a-5081-b2ed-2bace2a15a45" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e494b272-971a-5081-b2ed-2bace2a15a45" :answer/value "-6"] [:db/ensure "e494b272-971a-5081-b2ed-2bace2a15a45" :answer/validate] [:db/add "8b4e57b5-5c3e-5647-8168-db37d9e9f456" :answer/id #uuid "8b4e57b5-5c3e-5647-8168-db