-8f19-810a7454deec"] [:db/add "0905f52b-1aee-5bea-8f19-810a7454deec" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/47/472d6130b8d885f7d053919197ccb8a2890ff142afa37c7f1741ae6826966039.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "0905f52b-1aee-5bea-8f19-810a7454deec" :question/worked-solution "First trace $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/ed/ed48daa17c0b9bd21a45911526e7d223438380df9dc41b6593de9bdd81538c43.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $6$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{6}{2}=3$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-3\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}+(-3\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-3\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-3$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "0905f52b-1aee-5bea-8f19-810a7454deec" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "0905f52b-1aee-5bea-8f19-810a7454deec" :question/answer-fields "5123eae5-e318-5696-be8e-3c2751d52511"] [:db/ensure "0905f52b-1aee-5bea-8f19-810a7454deec" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "0905f52b-1aee-5bea-8f19-810a7454deec"] [:db/add "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67" :answer/id #uuid "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67"] [:db/add "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67" :answer/value "-3"] [:db/ensure "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67" :answer/validate] [:db/add "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e"] [:db/add "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e" :answer-field/choices "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67"] [:db/add "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e" :answer-field/correct "bf0562b8-d316-531b-af8c-56a8e36c6d67"] [:db/ensure "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db" :question/id #uuid "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db"] [:db/add "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/0d/0d2e1ca9aa7f9d8cd02bafb71ae33fa88eab3f0de7e2c1abb6f2b295a5b0a2d0.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db" :question/worked-solution "First trace $3\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/97/9704e966c216f2ad6a7d44c510761dad0785b2e0cbf83d3cb5030cefd5e922ee.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $6$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{6}{2}=3$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-3\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+(-3\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-3\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-3$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db" :question/answer-fields "3cbdf526-8cb6-520e-a048-6e2df1afcb6e"] [:db/ensure "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "f065bf4d-42af-52ee-a48e-0ee8fcbee8db"] [:db/add "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758" :answer/id #uuid "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758"] [:db/add "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758" :answer/value "-2"] [:db/ensure "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758" :answer/validate] [:db/add "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b"] [:db/add "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b" :answer-field/choices "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758"] [:db/add "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b" :answer-field/correct "2afc41a0-fb8d-53af-a7d3-44267dc50758"] [:db/ensure "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3" :question/id #uuid "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3"] [:db/add "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/74/74e0f3497892aeda037d5aadaa57fdbb1f38d492b14e7977550f14c6330c6822.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3" :question/worked-solution "First trace $3\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/7a/7a5036650f84013328da57fbc60eba029b45a30b5d8166dc6c24cfed9e0ff175.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $4$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{4}{2}=2$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-2\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+(-2\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-2\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-2$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3" :question/answer-fields "bfc6c478-efd1-54e2-8ece-9658e97d662b"] [:db/ensure "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "df910369-e57e-53f2-92c7-597b56fc17b3"] [:db/add "a950d4de-3d97-56a2-a570-ce43c8786d74" :answer/id #uuid "a950d4de-3d97-56a2-a570-ce43c8786d74"] [:db/add "a950d4de-3d97-56a2-a570-ce43c8786d74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "a950d4de-3d97-56a2-a570-ce43c8786d74" :answer/value "-4"] [:db/ensure "a950d4de-3d97-56a2-a570-ce43c8786d74" :answer/validate] [:db/add "7e73591f-fe73-53ae-8ea6-efc161bf3e82" :answer/id #uuid "7e73591f-fe73-53ae-8ea6-efc161bf3e82"] [:db/add "7e73591f-fe73-53ae-8ea6-efc161bf3e82" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "7e73591f-fe73-53ae-8ea6-efc161bf3e82" :answer/value "-12"] [:db/ensure "7e73591f-fe73-53ae-8ea6-efc161bf3e82" :answer/validate] [:db/add "97ad8a4e-5b21-59d3-ac08-a8709b8dda8c" :answer/id #uuid "97ad8a4e-5b21-59d3-ac