] [:db/add "6f754d54-7329-5642-9120-a40fc3e44f25" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/72/727161781a107f88462ea3304620d9e56e09e450717fd01239bf4da97923de8d.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "6f754d54-7329-5642-9120-a40fc3e44f25" :question/worked-solution "First trace $4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/9c/9ce74337e8c8db8e835392d2f253ecc2aef88603212059fedc079cb16f7a9a4e.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $12$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{12}{4}=3$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-3\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=4\\mathbf{b}+(-3\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-3\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-3$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "6f754d54-7329-5642-9120-a40fc3e44f25" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "6f754d54-7329-5642-9120-a40fc3e44f25" :question/answer-fields "bc70c4a7-d2c9-5eec-b2c7-90e7ae37be4a"] [:db/ensure "6f754d54-7329-5642-9120-a40fc3e44f25" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "6f754d54-7329-5642-9120-a40fc3e44f25"] [:db/add "01ac85fe-904c-51b2-a1bb-c9205eef834b" :answer/id #uuid "01ac85fe-904c-51b2-a1bb-c9205eef834b"] [:db/add "01ac85fe-904c-51b2-a1bb-c9205eef834b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "01ac85fe-904c-51b2-a1bb-c9205eef834b" :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{3}"] [:db/ensure "01ac85fe-904c-51b2-a1bb-c9205eef834b" :answer/validate] [:db/add "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d" :answer/id #uuid "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d"] [:db/add "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d" :answer/value "-4"] [:db/ensure "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d4194278-3edd-5061-b5e9-3948c6211a64" :answer/id #uuid "d4194278-3edd-5061-b5e9-3948c6211a64"] [:db/add "d4194278-3edd-5061-b5e9-3948c6211a64" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d4194278-3edd-5061-b5e9-3948c6211a64" :answer/value "-16"] [:db/ensure "d4194278-3edd-5061-b5e9-3948c6211a64" :answer/validate] [:db/add "797d5bc8-79ca-5401-a9bc-20cd56ee5e4a" :answer/id #uuid "797d5bc8-79ca-5401-a9bc-20cd56ee5e4a"] [:db/add "797d5bc8-79ca-5401-a9bc-20cd56ee5e4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "797d5bc8-79ca-5401-a9bc-20cd56ee5e4a" :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{4}"] [:db/ensure "797d5bc8-79ca-5401-a9bc-20cd56ee5e4a" :answer/validate] [:db/add "b7a92ed5-5d3e-5676-b8e4-8dc05e180c85" :answer/id #uuid "b7a92ed5-5d3e-5676-b8e4-8dc05e180c85"] [:db/add "b7a92ed5-5d3e-5676-b8e4-8dc05e180c85" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "b7a92ed5-5d3e-5676-b8e4-8dc05e180c85" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}"] [:db/ensure "b7a92ed5-5d3e-5676-b8e4-8dc05e180c85" :answer/validate] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/id #uuid "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/choices "01ac85fe-904c-51b2-a1bb-c9205eef834b"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/choices "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/choices "d4194278-3edd-5061-b5e9-3948c6211a64"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/choices "797d5bc8-79ca-5401-a9bc-20cd56ee5e4a"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/choices "b7a92ed5-5d3e-5676-b8e4-8dc05e180c85"] [:db/add "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/correct "2762a6ce-772b-51cf-acd1-a3d4a005208d"] [:db/ensure "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb" :question/id #uuid "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb"] [:db/add "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/1f/1f60c5d8c72737d7e21ecf71eb66fca62cc58ec622d41cfd86acee64ea23d86a.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb" :question/worked-solution "First trace $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/45/452184690634ad20749bf467bb3f491d93664c31760d82c6ac5087049b1bec1d.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $16$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{16}{4}=4$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-4\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}+(-4\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-4$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb" :question/answer-fields "45155574-a03a-5b83-b427-d30816f69958"] [:db/ensure "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "a058385f-3fe5-5ed0-bc2e-cd77849083eb"] [:db/add "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997" :answer/id #uuid "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997"] [:db/add "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997" :answer/value "-1"] [:db/ensure "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae" :answer-field/id #uuid "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae"] [:db/add "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae" :answer-field/choices "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997"] [:db/add "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae" :answer-field/correct "d252b653-2700-5f8d-804c-dba0ef752997"] [:db/ensure "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061" :question/id #uuid "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061"] [:db/add "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/04/0425a3cd22f183ef02768acf38ce10ea4c1b5f73722f718ead878b2ef230a4ff.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061" :question/worked-solution "First trace $3\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/a0/a0e3e19b1ca51ba09da116914e7c11bf155f01c2a4360f4956c28280491f9a1b.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $2$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{2}{2}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061" :question/answer-fields "ba4f0b94-f753-5d4b-9f21-dd63f2c2b9ae"] [:db/ensure "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "08d70796-c997-57db-a8ed-490cb432e061"] [:db/ensure 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/validate]]
